{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["The meaning of <b>ויגוע</b>: it is already <b>גוע</b>, and there are many like it in the Torah, such as <b>ואתחנן</b> (Deuteronomy 3:23), and likewise 'He rained down upon them manna' (Psalms 78:24), according to the true interpretation." "The word <b>ויגוע</b> [means] death, and in the verse 'he expired and died' (Genesis 25:5) I shall explain this to you. Now it is clear to you that the word <b>רמש</b> is a general term for birds and beasts and wild animals and creeping things that are small, and for man. And it is possible that 'all in whose nostrils was the breath of the spirit of life' refers back to man, for we do not find <b>נשמה</b> except for the breath of man, and many said it is so called because it is from the heavens [שמים], and if they are two roots, one may find its like."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:41.947220943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}